{"title":"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Bridget bought a bag of apples at the grocery store. She gave half of the apples to Ann. Then she gave Cassie 3 apples, keeping 4 apples for herself. How many apples did Bridget buy? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c32f8ef964125f813e4df616d16d04aabe9743.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 4\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 7\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 11\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"369\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we set up an equation, we find out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/151ebad2056e12d9ce9fee64d878b437b3111c31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=(3+4)\\cdot 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" /> because 3 apples were left after giving half, then four away. \nWe can simplify the equations to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c742a9821aabdc1c88ba68298bc9bec706a4cb01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=7\\cdot 2=14.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"115\" height=\"14\" />\nThe answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/3793efc5b382f403727e386c8b41bcc0b0512cef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(E) } 14.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>~John0412\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You can work backwards and add 3 apples that she gave to Cassie to the 4 she currently has, which results in 7, and then multiply by 2 since she gave half the apples to Ann, resulting in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d4f8e30b86ffdde17730169af2c90f48d206a52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nOr you can use algebra: let x be the number of apples, \nwe have 3+4+x/2 = x\nsolving for x, we get 14 resulting in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d4f8e30b86ffdde17730169af2c90f48d206a52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />. \n~Anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=USVVURBLaAc\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=USVVURBLaAc</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/a2-76knCCEE\">https://youtu.be/a2-76knCCEE</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"back